ine",\n        "description": "The DEBISA pipeline starts with preprocessing (loading data, handling missing values, normalizing, splitting sets), then initializes a population of binary masks. Fitness evaluation broadcasts the data and computes nearest‑neighbour error for each chromosome in parallel. Selection picks the fittest chromosome, applies crossover/mutation, and enforces a target reduction rate by fixing the proportion of zeros. This loop repeats until the desired number of generations or convergence, after which the best chromosome is collected and the reduced dataset can be exported as a new DataFrame."\n    },\n    {\n        "title": "Interpreting Results & Tips",\n        "description": "DEBISA outputs a binary vector indicating kept instances. Key metrics are reduction rate, classification accuracy (often measured with 1‑NN on the reduced set), and computation time. Typical results show 50‑75\u202f% reduction with minimal accuracy loss, running in hours on terabyte‑scale data with a 50‑node cluster. Tips include using a small number of cores per executor to avoid skew, tuning population size, and relaxing the reduction rate or adding a post‑pruning step if accuracy drops sharply."\n    }\n]'}, artifact_delta={}, transfer_to_agent=None, escalate=None, requested_auth_configs={}, requested_tool_confirmations={}, compaction=None, end_of_agent=None, agent_state=None, rewind_before_invocation_id=None, route=None, render_ui_widgets=None, set_model_response=None) output=None node_info=NodeInfo(path='', output_for=None, message_as_output=None) long_running_tool_ids=None branch=None isolation_scope=None id='64ede1ca-7c15-4d65-9d8d-d90123b19ac1' timestamp=1789026653.5717664
