In the preprocessing module, we first build an index for each instance 
and partition the entire data set into several subsets evenly according to 
the index. Each partitioned subset is treated as an independent popu­
lation. Next, we design a hash table to record the mapping relationship 
between gene and instances. We adopted the average partitioning to 
avoid the data skewness problem that a few machines afford most of the 
computing task while others are in idle state. Besides, these populations 
are independent in DEBISA to avoid data transmission among pop­
ulations and reduce the time costs caused by shuffle. 4.1.1. Build index and partition population 
