In this section, we first introduce the optimization strategies of 
DEBISA, then present the complete DEBISA. 3.1. The distributed coarse granularity chromosome structure 
As discussed in Section 1, the classic chromosome structure leads to a 
huge search space in big data environment. We apply two main ways to 
reduce the size of search space. The first one is to divide the original 
search space into several parallel sub-space, and the other is to change 
the granularity of each gene to reduce the length of a chromosome. If a 
gene represents more instances, its granularity is coarser; otherwise, its 
granularity is finer. For a non-time-series data set, each instance is a 
record about an independent truth, which means that there is no cau­

